expr main <([I, you, he, she, it, we, they, who] wont), (wont)>

let message "Did you mean the contraction `won't` (will not)?"
let description "After a pronoun, `wont` is almost always a missing apostrophe in `won't`."
let kind "Spelling"
let becomes "won't"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "She wont come tonight." "She won't come tonight."
test "I wont be late." "I won't be late."
test "He wont say a word." "He won't say a word."
test "They wont mind." "They won't mind."
test "We wont know until Friday." "We won't know until Friday."
test "you wont believe it." "you won't believe it."
test "It wont work." "It won't work."
test "Who wont help us?" "Who won't help us?"
test "She said he wont go." "She said he won't go."
test "I think they wont arrive." "I think they won't arrive."

allows "She won't come tonight."
allows "It was his wont to rise early."
allows "As is her wont, she arrived early."
allows "He is wont to complain."
allows "The wont of the people was clear."
